# Fixed 2026-11-13, defect 2492, lane b34-signals: a Heroes function C calls
# back on a thread C started itself.
# Symptom: the refusal named the function and the thread, then cited
# `design.md Part 7.13`, a file the program's reader does not have, and said
# nothing of what to write instead; both answers of panel 246's blind reading
# for a first thread task met it, each wrapping `pthread_create`.
# Cause: the guard at the entry of a function C may call spoke of the danger
# and not of the doors; it now names them in its own words, a thread started
# with `hero_thread_spawn` for work and C rather than a Heroes function for a
# signal. The refusal itself is panel 111's R9, unchanged: `worker` never runs.

extern "fixedbugs-2492-a-thread-of-cs-own.h"
    function foreign_call(body: (function(i64) -> i64)) -> i64

function worker(n: i64) -> i64
    print("worker ran with ", n)
    return n

function main()
    print("handing C the worker")
    print(foreign_call(body: worker))
